WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.565 --> 00:00:16.966
Morb groaned as he returned to consciousness.

2
00:00:17.726 --> 00:00:21.147
For a moment he didn't remember where he was or what had happened.

3
00:00:21.827 --> 00:00:25.909
Then he saw the ruined house around him and the heavy beam lying beside him.

4
00:00:26.589 --> 00:00:27.910
His memory came rushing back.

5
00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:32.652
"Aargh!" he yelled, gnashing his teeth.

6
00:00:33.408 --> 00:00:37.651
"Those rotten children will pay for making a fool of me yet again!"

7
00:00:38.751 --> 00:00:41.213
He rubbed his hands together and healed his aching head.

8
00:00:41.953 --> 00:00:44.354
Then he zapped himself back to the fortress.

9
00:00:45.215 --> 00:00:50.138
Several trolls were in the tower room staring dully at the map above the Secret Eye, as Morb

10
00:00:50.178 --> 00:00:50.678
had ordered.

11
00:00:51.438 --> 00:00:53.880
Morb glanced at the map, which was still blank.

12
00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:56.301
"Ridiculous," he snapped.

13
00:00:57.042 --> 00:01:00.724
Stalking over, he yanked the blink images out of the eye sockets.

14
00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:04.541
Immediately the map filled with glowing red dots.

15
00:01:05.421 --> 00:01:08.222
Morb glared at the trolls, who looked vaguely surprised.

16
00:01:08.242 --> 00:01:11.203
"Don't just stand there looking stupid!"

17
00:01:11.583 --> 00:01:12.123
he told them.

18
00:01:12.143 --> 00:01:14.723
"Go bring me some more Reds."

19
00:01:15.504 --> 00:01:17.004
The trolls exchanged a glance.

20
00:01:17.864 --> 00:01:21.685
One grunted, an image of sloppy gruel appearing over its head.

21
00:01:21.705 --> 00:01:25.586
"You'll get more food when you've earned it," Morb snapped.

22
00:01:26.847 --> 00:01:31.348
"Go!" He waited until the trolls zapped away, and then stomped downstairs.

23
00:01:32.192 --> 00:01:34.814
Boz was lying in his cell, weak and pale.

24
00:01:35.475 --> 00:01:40.779
Two trolls were coming out of the cell, carrying a large cauldron full of the bright blue leeches.

25
00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:45.283
"I hope you enjoyed today's treatment," Morb said sarcastically.

26
00:01:46.063 --> 00:01:51.368
"Normally I give my guests a day off to regain their magical energy between treatments.

27
00:01:52.068 --> 00:01:57.312
But since you are a former Magic Master, I thought you could handle two days in a row."

28
00:01:58.413 --> 00:02:01.596
Boz barely had the energy to lift his head and glare at Morb.

29
00:02:02.456 --> 00:02:05.198
"You won't get away with this," he croaked.

30
00:02:05.818 --> 00:02:09.960
"Don't try to talk too much, my friend," Morb warned with a sneer.

31
00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:12.862
"You need to rest before your next treatment.

32
00:02:13.362 --> 00:02:15.223
My leeches are always hungry.

33
00:02:16.004 --> 00:02:21.147
If you don't provide enough magic, they just might suck the life out of you one of these

34
00:02:21.227 --> 00:02:24.829
times." "Is that supposed to be a threat?"

35
00:02:25.189 --> 00:02:25.729
Boz said.

36
00:02:25.749 --> 00:02:28.971
"Because you don't scare me, Morb.

37
00:02:29.291 --> 00:02:30.032
You never did."

38
00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:36.603
"We'll see if you're still so confident when your grandson is in the cell next to you," Morb

39
00:02:36.663 --> 00:02:38.304
snarled. "Zann?"

40
00:02:38.704 --> 00:02:40.545
Panic suddenly filled Boz's face.

41
00:02:40.565 --> 00:02:42.086
"Is he here?"

42
00:02:42.827 --> 00:02:43.727
Morb didn't answer.

43
00:02:44.448 --> 00:02:49.610
Instead he turned and walked out of the cell, ordering the trolls to bring the cauldron of leeches.

44
00:02:50.671 --> 00:02:55.814
Boz continued to yell, but Morb ignored him and went into a small room at the end of

45
00:02:55.834 --> 00:02:56.454
the corridor.

46
00:02:57.635 --> 00:03:01.221
Inside was a stone pit full of firewood and kindling.

47
00:03:02.062 --> 00:03:04.884
Morb pointed, and instantly flames leaped out.

48
00:03:05.585 --> 00:03:08.747
With a grunt the trolls lifted the cauldron onto the fire.

49
00:03:09.508 --> 00:03:14.272
As the leeches cooked, the magic energy they had just ingested left their bodies.

50
00:03:15.393 --> 00:03:19.616
It rose up like steam, emerging from the cauldron in thick blue spirals.

51
00:03:20.557 --> 00:03:23.980
Morb leaned over the cauldron, breathing in the escaping magic.

52
00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:28.744
The steam burned his nose and throat, but he ignored the unpleasant feeling.

53
00:03:29.452 --> 00:03:32.954
For now he would continue to do things the slow, difficult way.

54
00:03:33.335 --> 00:03:34.375
But not for much longer.

55
00:03:35.156 --> 00:03:38.758
He was almost strong enough to put the next step of his plan into action.

56
00:03:38.778 --> 00:03:48.004
"Yes," he whispered, inhaling deeply, as more and more magical energy filled him.

57
00:03:48.805 --> 00:03:51.467
He felt powerful—more powerful than ever before.

58
00:03:52.227 --> 00:03:54.089
Boz had strong magic indeed.

59
00:03:54.629 --> 00:03:55.910
And now it was all his!

60
00:03:56.770 --> 00:03:58.912
Morb breathed in the last of the blue steam.

61
00:03:59.596 --> 00:04:05.939
Then he threw back his head and laughed, never noticing the big-eyed insect fluttering outside the tiny barred

62
00:04:05.999 --> 00:04:07.779
window at the top of the stone wall.

63
00:04:07.799 --> 00:04:12.761
"So your grandfather was suspicious of Morb from the start?"

64
00:04:13.082 --> 00:04:13.722
Gliss asked.

65
00:04:14.482 --> 00:04:15.943
Zann looked around at his friends.

66
00:04:16.663 --> 00:04:19.084
All of them, plus Zing, were still in the Hollow.

67
00:04:19.704 --> 00:04:21.105
They hadn't heard from Jev yet.

68
00:04:21.865 --> 00:04:25.547
So Zann was still reading as much as he could from his grandfather's diary.

69
00:04:25.567 --> 00:04:28.668
"Boz was suspicious of Morb," he said.

70
00:04:29.708 --> 00:04:31.509
"At least that's what he wrote in here.

71
00:04:32.309 --> 00:04:38.192
Boz stopped by the university a few days after Morb started working as an assistant animal caretaker at

72
00:04:38.252 --> 00:04:39.232
my parents' lab.

73
00:04:40.113 --> 00:04:43.534
At first Boz just thought Morb seemed secretive and shifty."

74
00:04:43.554 --> 00:04:44.975
"And then what?"

75
00:04:45.295 --> 00:04:45.915
Perda asked.

76
00:04:46.816 --> 00:04:53.398
"One day Boz caught Morb performing some nasty secret research on the lab animals," he said.

77
00:04:54.299 --> 00:04:55.039
Perda gasped.

78
00:04:55.059 --> 00:04:56.820
"What was he doing?"

79
00:04:57.664 --> 00:05:03.126
"Boz guessed that Morb was trying to figure out ways to steal magic from the creatures under his

80
00:05:03.186 --> 00:05:05.347
care." Darb looked stricken.

81
00:05:05.367 --> 00:05:06.608
"That's terrible!"

82
00:05:06.988 --> 00:05:09.449
he said, reaching out to stroke Zing's scales.

83
00:05:09.469 --> 00:05:14.271
"That sort of experimentation is strictly regulated by the Red Council.

84
00:05:14.971 --> 00:05:17.833
And caretakers are never supposed to take part in it."

85
00:05:18.993 --> 00:05:20.394
"I know," Zann said.

86
00:05:20.414 --> 00:05:22.575
"But I guess Morb didn't care.

87
00:05:23.455 --> 00:05:27.506
The second time Boz caught him, he was eating some leeches."

88
00:05:27.526 --> 00:05:29.247
"Eating them?"

89
00:05:29.707 --> 00:05:30.408
Gliss shuddered.

90
00:05:30.428 --> 00:05:33.030
"Yuck!" Zann nodded.

91
00:05:33.050 --> 00:05:35.612
"I guess it worked, at least a little.

92
00:05:36.373 --> 00:05:41.077
Morb was able to do enough magic to zap himself away before Boz could stop him."

93
00:05:42.178 --> 00:05:43.098
"What did Boz do?"

94
00:05:43.399 --> 00:05:43.979
Darb asked.

95
00:05:43.999 --> 00:05:48.603
"He told my parents that they should fire Morb and report him to the Council."

96
00:05:48.623 --> 00:05:51.145
"Did they?"

97
00:05:51.165 --> 00:05:54.368
"The next few pages aren't in very good shape."

98
00:05:55.152 --> 00:05:56.073
Zann bit his lip.

99
00:05:56.093 --> 00:05:58.474
"So I'm not sure what happened after that.

100
00:05:59.275 --> 00:06:03.718
The next part that's readable talks about Boz and me moving to Swamp Bottom."

101
00:06:05.039 --> 00:06:07.020
"Wow." Perda looked thoughtful.

102
00:06:07.040 --> 00:06:12.484
"Don't you find it odd that all that stuff happened right before your parents disappeared?"

103
00:06:13.244 --> 00:06:14.245
Zann shot her a look.

104
00:06:14.585 --> 00:06:18.308
"Are you saying that Morb had something to do with my parents' disappearance too?"

105
00:06:19.008 --> 00:06:22.271
Just then they heard Jev calling them from outside the Hollow.

106
00:06:22.991 --> 00:06:24.092
Perda jumped to her feet.

107
00:06:24.809 --> 00:06:27.135
"The spy fly must be back," she cried.

108
00:06:27.155 --> 00:06:29.421
"Let's go find out what it saw!"
